# state: first-run   (NFS MW has no golden profile, so every run is first-run)
# Need for Speed: Most Wanted (4541007B), lane.perdrawon1010: the race start the owner measured on 10-09.
# Quick Race -> Custom Race -> Sprint, default track (Diamond & Union), Opponents 2 (3 racers), Fiat Grande
# Punto, Auto: every menu step read from frames (passes 1-3, 1-1791641530-perdrawon1010-3932477,
# 1-1791642016-perdrawon1010-4029199, 1-1791643217-perdrawon1010-95991). Twelve race starts per boot: the
# first after the menus, eleven more by STANDINGS (d-pad up) -> Y Restart -> OK (the prompt opens on Cancel).
# Timing, from pass 3's frames: GO comes ~21 s after the transmission A (21.0 and 21.6 s in passes 3 and 2)
# and ~4.1 s after a restart's OK (4.2, 4.2, 4.0 s; a restart does not reload, the countdown runs at once).
# Each start holds RT (gas) from before GO, writes `mark gameplay` (first) or `mark go<N>` ~1.5 s BEFORE GO
# so the mark's screencap is done before the race starts, drives ~11 s past GO, shoots a frame, lets go.
# startread.py (docs/lanes/perdrawon1010/) reads the 10 s after GO as mark + 1.5 .. mark + 12.
wait 13.3
shot s01-publisher_logo
# step 1 [publisher_logo] This is an early boot logo animation (green polygon emblem on white), before any title or menu. No p
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 11.0
shot s02-intro_video
# step 2 [intro_video] The previous step was a publisher logo, and this is a cinematic-style showcase with no menu or promp
press START 120
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 10.4
shot s03-intro_video
# step 3 [intro_video] Static EA title art with a copyright line and no menu or prompt yet, so it is not gameplay. The prev
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 6.8
